  "analysis": "We will implement a memory-efficient bitmask DP in C++17 to decide feasibility. It uses dp[mask][last] encoded as a 1D array of floats to keep memory around 80MB for the worst-case (1<<20)*20 floats. Distances are computed with hypot. The strict inequality dist(H->i) < dist(D,i) and time + dist(last,i) < dist(D,i) are enforced with a small epsilon.",
